- op: discuss  # 169d
  at: '2026-08-31T11:36:32Z'  # 169d
  by: agent  # 169d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 169d
  clock: 5  # 169d
  nonce: 169d  # 169d
  message: "VALIDATED BY THE LEG THAT REPORTED THE BREAK, AND THE COMMIT WAS CHECKED RATHER\nTHAN THE COLOUR.\n\nThis item was left `pending_validation` deliberately, on the rule that a nightly\nverdict you happen to read may PREDATE the fix. Checked both halves:\n\n  nightly cron, all four matrix legs: success at 17d67608\n    leg 1 is python 3.10 (.woodpecker/nightly.yml `matrix.python: [\"3.10\", ...]`)\n    https://ci.revolving-tactile.com.de/repos/1/pipeline/2029/1\n  the fix is 9e3a2e7127 \"fix(py310): guard the tomllib import and declare the\n    tomli backport\"\n  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 9e3a2e7127 17d67608` -> TRUE\n\nSo the green leg ran WITH the fix in the tree, on the exact interpreter that\nrecorded `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tomllib'` against 2905 failed\ntests and 124 errors. That is behavioural evidence on the production path, not a\nproxy: the item's statement is about whether hypergumbo runs on its declared\nminimum, and the run that answers it is the one that previously did not.\n\nWHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. This validates the ONE import that broke. It does not\nvalidate that no other 3.11+ symbol has entered the tree since -- the standing\nguard for that is `test_stdlib_version_guarded_imports.py`, which the earlier\nentry disclosed is selected by no top-level source and therefore runs on\n`full-suite` twice daily rather than per-PR. That gap is disclosed on its own\nterms and is not closed here."  # 169d
